Usage: mktemp [OPTION]... [TEMPLATE]

Create a temporary file or directory, safely, and print its name.

TEMPLATE must contain at least 3 consecutive 'X's in last component.
If TEMPLATE is not specified, use tmp.XXXXXXXXXX instead.

Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

Note: This implementation uses Windows GetTempFileName API.
Custom templates are partially supported.

OPTIONS:
  -d, --directory   make a directory instead of a file
  -u, --dry-run     do not actually create anything
  -q, --quiet       suppress diagnostics
      --suffix ARG  append SUFFIX to TEMPLATE; SUFFIX must not contain a path
                    separator
  -t                interpret TEMPLATE as a single file name component, relative
                    to a directory
  -p, --tmpdir ARG  interpret TEMPLATE relative to DIR; if DIR is not specified,
                    use $TMPDIR
      --help        display this help and exit
  -V, --version     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
